---
// AppPage — the reusable full-height content frame for prototype screens inside
// AppShell. It pins natural-height sections (a page title, a filter card) at the
// top and lets the LAST child (a workspace / grid / map) fill the shell's scroll
// area with its own internal scroll. Any prototype composes:
//   <AppShell><AppPage> …sections… </AppPage></AppShell>
// so the page itself carries ZERO layout CSS.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: the full-height app-frame spine (flex column, spacing-600
// gutter, last-child fills) — no stack/grid layout primitive expresses
// fill-height-with-a-growing-last-child. A reusable layout, not a reinvented UI
// primitive.
---

<div class="app-page"><slot /></div>

<style>
  .app-page {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-400, 16px);
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 0;
    padding: var(--spacing-600, 32px);
  }
  /* The last section (a workspace/explorer) claims the remaining height and runs
     its own internal scroll; earlier sections keep their natural height. */
  .app-page > :global(:last-child) {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
  }
</style>
